#PHASES DRAFT 

I host client websites manually on a VPS. Every new client means repeating the
same setup by hand — provision the server, configure NGINX, set up SSL, write
firewall rules, deploy the app. It is slow, easy to get wrong, and inconsistent
between clients. If a server dies, rebuilding is a scramble.

## The solution

Codify that entire setup in Terraform so a complete, secured client environment
stands up from a single command — and tears down just as cleanly.

**Terraform makes the infrastructure reproducible. Docker makes the application
deployment reproducible.** Together, every client environment comes up identical.

