## Cost approach

The Terraform code is the artifact — the infrastructure does not need to run
continuously. `terraform destroy` runs whenever the stack is not being actively
tested or demonstrated, keeping spend near zero. Billing alarms are configured at
$5 and $20.

NAT gateway (~$32/month) is disabled by default. VPC endpoints for ECR are the
cheaper and more appropriate alternative for pulling container images.

## Deliberately out of scope

**Kubernetes.** Docker on EC2 with an autoscaling group maps directly onto the
VPS workflow being replaced and keeps the before-and-after story clear. ECS or
Fargate would be the more modern choice; that tradeoff is documented rather than
hidden.
